    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Linode VPS Review 2026: $5/mo Nanode to $192/mo Plans</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Published 2026-08-08 · Developer-favorite cloud since 2003, Akamai-powered since 2022 · Verified plan data from Akamai techdocs + independent 2026 testing</p>

    <div class="bg-gray-900 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold">4.5/5</span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">Developer Rating</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        Linode is the quiet workhorse of the developer cloud market — running continuously since 2003 and now backed by Akamai for the three years since the $900M acquisition in 2022. The pitch has not changed: a transparent $5/mo Nanode entry, hourly or monthly billing, 40Gbps networking, and a documentation + API ecosystem that is still the benchmark for the industry. In 2026, Linode remains one of the most dependable defaults for a full-stack developer who just wants a VPS to work, at a fair price, without billing surprises.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4">Quick Specs and Judgment</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      The shared CPU line (the "Linodes" most buyers mean when they say Linode) starts at the Nanode 1GB for $5/mo and scales to a 32GB plan at $192/mo. Every shared plan carries the same 40Gbps network uplink and the same transparent pricing model: what you see at signup is what you pay at renewal. The whole shared range supports hourly billing, so a scratch instance for a deploy or a benchmark costs only pennies.
    </p>
